Package.json is the configuration for npm
npm is a package manager but don't have a full form
Bundler like webpack bundles your code so that it can be pushed to production
^ minor upgrade will be installae automatically
~ major version upgrade will be installed automatically
package-lock.json keep an exact track of version of packages
node modules contains all the code npm fetches for a package while installing
Transitive Dependencies are there in node modules 
There are dev depnecies installed with npm install -D parcel
There are also production dependencies 
Transitive depnedencies -> Like all dependencies have their own package.json having their own dependecies 
npm init creates the package.json
npx parcel index.html -> Igniting the App
npm install installs the package
npx executes the package
React is a Javascript code hosted on npm
CDN links is not a preferred way to bring React 
npm install React
Parcle creates Dev buils, starts local server and also and Hot Module Replacement i.e anything chnaged page refreshes by itself
Parcel uses a file watching algorithm for HMR written in C++.
Parcel gives faster builds because of Caching in folder parcel-cache
parcel do image optimization also as most expensive thing is to load images 
Parcel compress, minify, bundle, consistent hashing, code splitting, good error handling, differential bundling
Parcel does Tree Shaking also that is remove Unused code
Parcel has a dev and prod build separatley
For production build npx parcel build index.html
For dev build : npx parcel index.html
browserslist -> compatible with browsers
npm run start or npm start same thing
in package.json check for start script to see the command to run the project 
npx is not needed because npm puts the node modules path at 0th position
React.create element just create objects which then ReactDom.render renders as html
JSX is just a javascript syntax 
JSX is not the html written inside Javascript but JSX is a html like syntax
JSX is not a valid Javascript as browser, js engines can't read this code 
JSX code is transpiled by Parcel(using Babel) before it reaches js engines
Babel is a Javascript Compiler -> Job to convert JSX to JS code
JSX --> Converted to React.createElement --> Then rendered as HTML
Parcel is like the manager of Babel.
html use class and jsx className
Attributes to JSX are given in camelCase
Wrap JSX in () if you are writing in multiple lines

React components two ways to write : 
Class Based components - OLD way 
Function Based components - NEW -> A Javascript function that returns some piece of JSX => Name Capital letter 

A functional Component rendered like root.render(< HeadingComponent />)
Rendering Component inside Component is called Component Composition.
JSX is a mix of HTML and Javascript.
You can write js in {} in JSX 
You can put ReactElement in ReactComponent or vice-versa or can do any sort of mix and match 
JSX takes care of injection attacks 
JSX stops cross-scripting attacks as it sanitizes the data whatever you write in {} in code 
You can call a Function also in JSX so basically React Components are also JS Functions and they can be called inside like functions inside JSX
In jsx we write inline css like :
const styleCard = {
    backgroundColor : "red"
}

<h1 style={styleCard}> So style has to be given like JS object

