--CLASS BASED COMPONENTS--

import React from "react";
class className extends React.Component {
    //Now class based component receives props in constructor
    costructor(props){
        //In JavaScript, before you can use this inside a child-class constructor, you must call the parent class constructor using super().
        super(props);
    }

    //This render function a classs have which basically returns the JSX to be coverted to HTML and rendered
    render(){
        return (
            <div>Name : {this.props.name}</div>
        )
    }
};
export default className

React.Component is a class provided by React and we are inheriting it 

Passing props
<User name={"deeksha"} />

In ckass bases components era we were not having hooks so 
class className extends React.Component {
    constructor(props){
        super(props);
        this.state = {
            count = 0,
            count2 = 1,
        }
    }

    render(){
        return (
            <h1>{this.state.count}</h1>
        )
