})

Also we can write 
import {Component} from "react"
clsass className extends Component

React class have a method :
componentDidMount(){ -> This is called when constructor run then render run then this for a class

}

Now remember the order also 
First Parent constructor called
Parent render will be called 
Child constructor will be called
Child render will be called 
Child didMount will be called
Parent DidMount will be called 

componentDidMout is used to make API call

React Lifecycel:
----------------
Has two phases : 
Render Phase : constructor run + render run
Commit Phase : componentDidMount callesd and actual DOM updated
If two children are there it optiimses by running Render phase for all childs first and then running Commit phase for both

ParentConstructro called
Parent render called

Child1 constructor
Child1 render

Child2 constructor
Child2 render

//DOM Updation in Single btach (Difference between Virtual dom and reconcilitation)
Child1 DidMount
Child2 DidMount

Parent didMount

for making an API call
async componentDidMount(){
    data = await fetch("url");
    const jsondata = await data.json()
}

componentDidUpdate

Now whole cycle: 
-----------------
Mounting cycle
--------------
parent constructor
parent render
child constructor 
child render

child didMount
this.setstate(API data) 
parent did Mounting
Mounting cycle finsihed

//Update cycle 
since state chnaged with new data
render will be called
componentDidUpdate will be called

in constructor may be 
this.times = setInterval({}=>{}, 1000)

Now ComponentWillUnmount(){
    clearInterval(this.timer) //this is shared across all ocmonents
} for cleanup like setInterval
When that compinent deaches like you move to new page

Unmounting in React useEffect
-----------------------------

useEffect(()=>{
   timer =  setInterval(()=>{}, 1000)
    //This return function will be called when the component will be unmounted
    return ()=>{
        clearInterval(timer)
    }
}, [])







